serana-post-training — third-party material and terms
=====================================================

The repository contains four kinds of material, and they are not under the
same terms. `LICENSE` (MIT) covers the first only.

1. Code — MIT
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Everything under `src/`, `scripts/`, `deploy/`, `demo/`, `config/`, plus
`main.py` and the documentation. Use it as you like under `LICENSE`.


2. Source dialogue — CC BY-SA
----------------------------------------------------------------------
The training corpora are derived from character dialogue on two wikis,
both of which publish under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike.
Section-level attribution is recorded in `config/data_sources.yaml`.

  UESP (primary)
    https://en.uesp.net/wiki/Skyrim:Serana
    Sections: Background, Quest-Related Events, Dialogue, Combat Dialogue,
    Follower Dialogue

  Elder Scrolls Wiki on Fandom (supplementary)
    https://elderscrolls.fandom.com/wiki/Serana
    Section: Quotes

ShareAlike applies downstream: text derived from these sources carries the
same licence and the same attribution requirement. That includes
`data/ko/cpt_corpus.txt` and the real-pair portion of the SFT set. Note
that 92.3% of the final SFT set is model-generated rather than wiki text
(README, "Data composition"), but the two are mixed in one file, so treat
the file as CC BY-SA rather than trying to separate them.


